    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d62">

                <pb facs="0178" n="62" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg62"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/937.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-01-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 19, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Imperial Clan voted today to accept the edict that Yuan has drafted, by which
                    the Emperor abdicates and consents to organization of republican government.</p>
                <p>Yuan will be made plenipotentiary to negotiate with revolutionists and organize a
                    new government. He intends to remove to Tientsin and there conduct the
                    Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Calhoun</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
